---
/**
 * The wheel strip that closes a case study.
 *
 * The Studio 1947 wheel rolls once from left to right along a rule, and as it
 * passes each of the six practice words those words gather out of loose
 * particles into place. It holds, scatters back, and runs again.
 *
 * Ported from the authored motion piece (Studio 1947 Footer): same geometry,
 * easing and timing, drawn on a canvas rather than through React so the page
 * ships no framework, no in-browser JSX compiler, and no per-frame DOM churn
 * for several thousand dots. Motion lives in scripts/footerStrip.ts.
 */
---

<div class="footer-strip" data-footer-strip>
  <canvas class="footer-strip__canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <p class="footer-strip__sr">
    Data, Design, Technology, Communication, Research, AI-ML Integration.
  </p>
</div>
